WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.852
Welcome.

2
00:00:02.352 --> 00:00:12.098
This short tour shows the Celebrate Recovery site of Orcas Island Community Church: a place for members to find help with their hurts, hang-ups, and habits.

3
00:00:15.021 --> 00:00:18.967
This site is for members, so it opens at the log-in page.

4
00:00:19.491 --> 00:00:27.494
The site's leaders set up your account. If you don't have one yet, press, No account yet? Email us to ask for one.

5
00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:32.811
Log in with your email address, or your phone number, and your password.

6
00:01:08.655 --> 00:01:19.724
The welcome page shows what is on the site: the Bible, daily devotionals, the lessons and guides of Celebrate Recovery, testimonies and songs, and books on Kindle.

7
00:01:20.237 --> 00:01:23.063
Each card has buttons to read or to search.

8
00:01:23.571 --> 00:01:29.787
The menu on the left takes you to every part of the site. Click a group to open it, and see its pages.

9
00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:34.407
Let's start with the Bible.

10
00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:38.963
Choose a Bible, a book, and a chapter, and press Go.

11
00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.791
Then just keep scrolling, to read on from chapter to chapter.

12
00:01:48.297 --> 00:01:59.501
Click a verse number for more about that verse: Show in Context, Other Translations, Related Verses, the original Hebrew or Greek words, and your own notes.

13
00:02:02.233 --> 00:02:03.933
You can also listen.

14
00:02:04.468 --> 00:02:09.480
Choose Listen from here on a verse, or press Listen beside a chapter's name.

15
00:02:10.019 --> 00:02:14.559
The verse being read is highlighted, and the reading carries on by itself.

16
00:02:19.019 --> 00:02:23.422
A bar at the foot lets you pause or stop, and choose the voice and the speed.

17
00:02:31.867 --> 00:02:35.678
Search the Bible for any words, or an exact phrase.

18
00:02:36.185 --> 00:02:39.549
Here we search for, my grace is sufficient.

19
00:02:43.488 --> 00:02:55.102
Every result has links: to the verse in context, the full chapter, other translations, related verses, and Download Card, which saves the verse as a picture to share.

20
00:02:57.887 --> 00:03:05.728
Search Everything looks through the Bible, the devotionals, the lessons and guides, the media, and the FAQ, all at once.

21
00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:12.703
A search for denial finds the verses first, then the readings and the lessons that talk about it.

22
00:03:17.985 --> 00:03:24.731
The devotionals open at today's date, with Streams in the Desert and Daily Strength for Daily Needs.

23
00:03:26.671 --> 00:03:33.154
Under them, On Kindle lists books in Amazon's Kindle reader, to read with your own Kindle account.

24
00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:47.895
Other books holds the Celebrate Recovery lessons: the leader's guides and lesson notes for all twenty-five lessons, the bulletin inserts, the Road to Recovery, the Twelve Steps, and more.

25
00:03:48.435 --> 00:03:51.586
Open one to read it, a chapter at a time.

26
00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:02.576
And you can search them all, for a word such as, amends.

27
00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:15.782
Christian media has the lesson videos, testimonies, and worship songs.

28
00:04:20.488 --> 00:04:23.488
Open one to play it, with its words below.

29
00:04:29.446 --> 00:04:33.677
And you can search the media, by title, or the words of a song.

30
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:48.295
The FAQ answers common questions about Celebrate Recovery, and about recovery based on the Bible.

31
00:04:48.809 --> 00:04:51.991
Choose a question, and press Show the answer.

32
00:04:53.129 --> 00:05:01.992
The answers are written by Google's Gemini A.I., with every Scripture reference as a link. The A.I. can make mistakes, and the page says so.

33
00:05:04.821 --> 00:05:11.589
Today, in the menu, has a Verse of the day: a Bible verse written over a photograph, new each time.

34
00:05:12.126 --> 00:05:15.711
Download the picture to share it, or press Show another.

35
00:05:18.023 --> 00:05:21.449
Devotional of the day does the same with today's reading.

36
00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:30.080
Under the verse of the day, Make your own card: choose a verse and a background, then download it, or send it to someone on the site.

37
00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.912
Your account

38
00:05:47.832 --> 00:05:53.374
The round icon at the top right of every page is your menu. Point at it to open it.

39
00:05:53.876 --> 00:05:59.640
Account settings is where you add your picture, which then shows in that icon. Only you see it.

40
00:06:02.651 --> 00:06:11.073
You can also give a cell phone number, choose whether your messages come by email, by text, or both, and ask for a verse a day.

41
00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.911
To stop texts at any time, reply STOP to any text.

42
00:06:18.645 --> 00:06:22.783
You can write your own notes on any verse, reading, or lesson.

43
00:06:23.284 --> 00:06:27.696
Click a verse number, choose Notes, write your note, and save it.

44
00:06:35.372 --> 00:06:42.656
My Notes, in the same menu, keeps every note in one place, with a search, and a link back to each one.

45
00:06:45.379 --> 00:06:51.594
Any devotional can be emailed to you each day, and texted too, if you asked for texts.

46
00:06:52.117 --> 00:06:55.747
Choose the time and your time zone, and press the button.

47
00:06:57.724 --> 00:07:02.234
You can change the time, or stop the emails, whenever you like.

48
00:07:04.999 --> 00:07:11.192
On the media page, tick the songs you want, give the list a name, and save it as a playlist.

49
00:07:21.929 --> 00:07:25.786
Then press Play, and the songs play one after another.

50
00:07:30.056 --> 00:07:36.953
Press Edit to change a playlist: drag a song to a new place, remove one, or add others from a list.

51
00:07:48.399 --> 00:07:50.923
Every search can keep what you find.

52
00:07:54.062 --> 00:07:58.255
Tick the results you want, give the list a name, and press Save.

53
00:08:06.166 --> 00:08:13.277
My Lists keeps each list, with a link back to every entry, and Copy to notes turns a whole list into a note.

54
00:08:26.192 --> 00:08:32.605
Every card you make and keep, download, or send is saved on My cards, in your account menu.

55
00:08:35.384 --> 00:08:41.692
Edit a card to change its verse or its background, download it again, or send it to someone.

56
00:08:44.433 --> 00:08:55.742
If you serve in a group, such as the Friday volunteers, My scheduled tasks, in your account menu, lists the days you are scheduled for, and whether each is confirmed.

57
00:08:56.276 --> 00:09:04.327
Add a task asks for one of your group's tasks, on a date you choose. It shows as not confirmed until your leader confirms it.

58
00:09:08.128 --> 00:09:12.367
Remove takes you off one, and your leader is emailed either way.

59
00:09:15.112 --> 00:09:16.645
Members together

60
00:09:19.563 --> 00:09:22.986
Conversations is where members share with one another.

61
00:09:23.901 --> 00:09:27.677
Members can reply, and write posts of their own.

62
00:09:36.142 --> 00:09:44.960
Posts should not contain profanity, political messages, or ads. Tick, Email me replies, to hear about each new reply.

63
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:51.520
Or choose one member under Send to, and only the two of you will see it.

64
00:09:55.164 --> 00:09:58.523
The Prayer Wall is for prayer requests and praises.

65
00:09:59.045 --> 00:10:03.901
Members share what they need prayer for, and others reply to say they are praying.

66
00:10:11.197 --> 00:10:24.324
Choose who sees each request: everyone, anonymously, only you and the site's leaders, or everyone on the weekly prayer list. If you are in a group, you can send it to your group, or just to its leader.

67
00:10:32.261 --> 00:10:36.227
When a prayer is answered, its author can mark it, Answered.

68
00:10:38.997 --> 00:10:44.620
And whenever you need it, the Help page is a full user guide, with pictures of every feature.

69
00:10:46.825 --> 00:10:52.477
This video is there, too, and the Privacy page says what the site keeps about you.

70
00:10:55.212 --> 00:10:56.884
Thank you for watching.

71
00:10:57.384 --> 00:10:59.294
We are glad you are here.
